{
    "word": "leporine",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "89782b35-fac8-3b1d-b56e-426423347fd6",
                "word": "leporine",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                        "entry_id": "89782b35-fac8-3b1d-b56e-426423347fd6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, relating to, or characteristic of a hare or a rabbit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "148e7be9-2205-4bbf-84d2-363aea7db430",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "His leporine ears perked up at the mention of dessert."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31040767-629e-4ec4-a03c-6c6d01d5eacc",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "This [the harp seal] inhabits the ſame countries vvith the Rough and Leporine Seal; but loves the coldeſt parts of the coaſt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e567622d-4ac2-48ab-a3a5-5caf212327be",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "Thus it is that one injustice generates another, and that the breed is propagated, with more than leporine fecundity, through every successive measure which these third-rate Legislators, these Statesmen in waiting, are sent to inflict upon Ireland."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a3dab59-2b83-4531-80b9-969e79515cec",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "[T]he fur [of the hispid hare] is very remarkable for an animal of the Leporine group, on account of its harshness, which is well expressed by the specific appellation hispidus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a204c18-74d5-4d8c-979a-3d3b6f6da6e1",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "I further give an anatomical systematic revision of the adult leporine tapeworms, together with their generic relationship to the cestodes of cattle, sheep, and horses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ff9c3d7-dd09-4a8d-8f58-d1f711b7a33d",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "Glad as she was to eat of the leporine family, she detested sport for sport's sake, even the fox-hunting, though her poultry-run had just been raided and a dog-fox had snarled fearlessly at Nip from the ditch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "347ac255-06c0-4264-836d-9588cc46212a",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "This is basic Peter Rabbit economics that everyone can understand [quoting Thomas G. Ayers]. / Having little faith in economists, even leporine ones, I propose to examine Ayers' thesis carefully."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb1f2889-0d89-4387-90d9-1a8854c98889",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "This curious passage begins with an intimation of a level of awareness in Uncle Remus, associated with his leporine \"quick ear,\" which allows him to shift from the \"senseless affair\" into \"a recitation of nonsense.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "556a3ade-ce0d-4934-b687-843c220c7070",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "Mr Todd launched into a forceful disquisition, […] At last he stopped and sat gazing at her with the same desperate, leporine look as before, audibly breathing, his lips drawn back in a sort of leer and those teeth on show again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70e83039-46fc-432f-b87c-1d8f8364b558",
                                "sense_id": "0bb34a78-5a51-38be-aad1-9dba8b7d8d6a",
                                "text": "The aforementioned rodent and leporine studies represented some of the first in vivo reports of intra-amniotic injection of fetal cells in mammals."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
